9. **Step 9a - T1 Template Selection** (Code, T1 branch) — a hash function (`Math.imul`-based) on `hsi_record_id` deterministically selects a template: filters `templates` by `t["Signal Category"] === dominant_pole` (defaulting to `"Negative"` if missing), falls back to the full pool if no match, then `pool[seed % pool.length]`. Sets `solution_type` (= selected `Template Name`, or `"Standard Response"`), `emotional_axis` (= enriched_emotion_tag, or a fallback), `signal_based_consideration` (= selected template's own field, or a fallback), **`tone_style` hardcoded to `"Empathetic-Warm"` for all T1 records regardless of context**, `urgency_level` (= urgency_level_default), **`commercial_risk_flag` hardcoded `false`**, **`governance_flag` hardcoded `"None"`** (subject to override in the next node), `behavioral_interpretation: null` (T1 never gets an LLM-generated interpretation), `t1_template_id` (= selected template's Id).
10. **Step 9b - T1 Governance Screen** (Code, T1 branch) — attempts to override `governance_flag` to `"Flag"` if `signal_type === 'Dignity-Risk Signal'` OR `pain_point_sub_category.includes("Trust, Dignity")`. **Confirmed likely bug, compound: (a) the `signal_type === 'Dignity-Risk Signal'` check is very likely structurally unreachable in this branch at all, since HSI's own tier logic already routes any `Dignity-Risk Signal` record to T3, never T1 — so a T1 record here can't actually have that signal type; (b) the `pain_point_sub_category.includes("Trust, Dignity")` check references the wrong field — `"Trust, Dignity"` is part of a canonical *domain* name (`pain_point_domain_confirmed`'s value `"Trust, Dignity & Belonging"`), not something that appears in `pain_point_sub_category` (a specific enriched pain-point phrase). This is the second confirmed occurrence of this exact same wrong-field bug pattern — HSI's own `Step 16` has an identical mistake — strong evidence of one bug propagated by copy-paste across two agents, not two independent errors. Net effect: this node's entire purpose (catching dignity/trust-risk signals that slipped into the low-severity T1 lane) is likely fully inert.**
11. **Step 9c - Build Claude Prompt** (Code, T2/T3 branch) — `bra_system_prompt` defines the role explicitly: **"You are the BRA (Brand Response Architect) agent"** (note: contradicts the baseline doc's "Brand Response Agent" — see Corrections). States the agent reasons about response strategy, does not draft language, does not classify emotion; governance principle that SubtextCX never prescribes operational actions, and that `signal_based_consideration` is internal guidance, not a directive. Demands exactly 7 JSON fields: `emotional_axis`, `signal_based_consideration`, `tone_style` (enum: `Empathetic-Formal`/`Empathetic-Warm`/`Neutral-Professional`/`Dignity-Restorative`), `urgency_level` (enum: `Immediate`/`Standard`/`Monitoring`), `commercial_risk_flag` (bool), `governance_flag` (enum: `None`/`Flag`/`Halt`), `behavioral_interpretation` (2-3 sentences). Explicit prohibition list for `signal_based_consideration`: refund amounts, vouchers, discounts, unauthorized promises, operational prescriptions. Tone guidance given for T3 (Dignity-Restorative), T2-Masked/Conflicted (Empathetic-Formal), T2-Ambiguous (Neutral-Professional) — **but other T2 triggers (plain Negative Signal at High/Moderate intensity, bare ambiguity_flag, interpretation_confidence Medium) aren't explicitly mapped to a tone, a minor prompt-completeness gap, not a hard failure since the enum still constrains output.** `governance_flag: "Halt"` triggers: discrimination/legal language, explicit escalation threat, unauthorized commitment. Language rule: if `lang: es`, translate `emotional_axis`/`signal_based_consideration`/`behavioral_interpretation` to Spanish. `bra_user_prompt` feeds: preliminary_response_tier, signal_type, intensity_level, pattern_type_recurrence, prior_record_count, lang, stability_axis, pain_axis, signal_synthesis_summary (labeled "HSI INTERPRETATION"), contextual_linguistic_framing (labeled "LINGUISTIC"), masked_emotion_hypothesis (conditional).
12. **Step 9d - Build Claude Request Body** (Code, T2/T3 branch) — `model: claude-sonnet-4-6, max_tokens: 500, temperature: 0.3`.

